                        "source_sense_id": "95d7fac8-cdf3-393e-b219-f5328b7a46c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "avaricious",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "avaricious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2dd7cb52-76dd-3012-884a-d42ed76aacc6",
                                        "entry_id": "aca2632c-5932-37db-b2e1-f6cab585f3ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Actuated by avarice; extremely greedy for wealth or material gain; immoderately desirous of accumulating property."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36ef926e-9a2b-4ed8-bbc0-994e371d17e1",
                                                "sense_id": "2dd7cb52-76dd-3012-884a-d42ed76aacc6",
                                                "text": "In a word, he was called a hard, avaricious, rapacious man, whose chief business was to enrich himself..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d1eeb926-7b5e-4ac7-905e-86fa5ef4bf41",
                        "source_entry_id": "df1918e4-7ce5-3e03-81f3-9540133b9f26",
                        "source_sense_id": "95d7fac8-cdf3-393e-b219-f5328b7a46c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "miserly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "miserly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1231507d-acf7-37cc-aaca-1309ae7e939a",
                                        "entry_id": "5b32250b-0425-35f0-a3bc-ae329005f30b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Like a miser, very or objectionably cautious with money."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "885e4d83-d434-4b77-88ba-7d67bb72b96f",
                                                "sense_id": "1231507d-acf7-37cc-aaca-1309ae7e939a",
                                                "text": "It's something that worries me about the book I'm doing about him... In some ways he's just like the racist caricature of the miserly old Jew."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4838c1c3-2e2e-46bf-884f-19d0a151f36e",
                                                "sense_id": "1231507d-acf7-37cc-aaca-1309ae7e939a",
                                                "text": "What could be more selfish, more miserly—this in specific is what gnaws at him—than dying childless, terminating the line, subtracting oneself from the great work of generation? Worse than miserly, in fact: unnatural."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7b5a6962-4986-4e46-a3ba-0cf2cd69aea9",
                        "source_entry_id": "df1918e4-7ce5-3e03-81f3-9540133b9f26",
                        "source_sense_id": "95d7fac8-cdf3-393e-b219-f5328b7a46c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "stingy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "stingy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95bd91d8-3472-3993-840e-233eff8ec12f",
                                        "entry_id": "29b0fb9c-648e-333d-ba04-0fe57197774a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Stinging; able or inclined to sting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b44ea69-23a0-4bc5-a62e-1a696778492b",
                                                "sense_id": "95bd91d8-3472-3993-840e-233eff8ec12f",
                                                "text": "Bumble bee – Bumble bee / I send to you this sonnet, / But please don't be – Bumble bee / The stingy bee in my bonnet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "stingy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9c4482f-cb8d-3088-aa45-ce4d0750f846",
                                        "entry_id": "41ef67e6-1f16-33fa-8d4f-48c9cf2a32e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unwilling to spend, give, or share; ungenerous; mean."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2922a777-259a-42cf-872b-2ed9c6285007",
                                                "sense_id": "b9c4482f-cb8d-3088-aa45-ce4d0750f846",
                                                "text": "\"Well, I'm doing my best to grow,\" said Davy, \"but it's a thing you can't hurry much. If Marilla wasn't so stingy with her jam I believe I'd grow a lot faster.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e4b0658-f8a5-32db-be97-6f7183924bf7",
                                        "entry_id": "41ef67e6-1f16-33fa-8d4f-48c9cf2a32e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Small, scant, meager, insufficient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "460e8246-7840-45f4-9e72-c3f8609b0cf0",
                                                "sense_id": "6e4b0658-f8a5-32db-be97-6f7183924bf7",
                                                "text": "The realization of this joint oppression is like discovering that the stingy crusts of bread being held out by society have mold on them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a14b458a-4d17-4e05-ae44-87491eba484c",
                                                "sense_id": "6e4b0658-f8a5-32db-be97-6f7183924bf7",
                                                "text": "As the moon wheels around Earth every 28 days and shows us a progressively greater and then stingier slice of its sun-lightened face, the distance between the moon and Earth changes, too. At the nearest point along its egg-shaped orbit, its perigee, the moon may be 26,000 miles closer to us than it is at its far point."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
